## Branch Naming
```
feat/issue-{N}-{short-slug}     new feature
fix/issue-{N}-{short-slug}      bug fix
chore/issue-{N}-{short-slug}    maintenance / deps
spike/issue-{N}-{short-slug}    investigation
```

## Commit Format (Conventional Commits)
```
feat(auth): add JWT refresh token endpoint
fix(auth): handle null user in token validation
test(auth): add integration tests for refresh flow
chore(deps): update Spring Security dependency
```
Link the issue in the PR body (`Closes #N`), not as a commit trailer.

Before every push: `git log -1` must show **no** tool attribution (`Co-authored-by` for agents, `Made with …`, vendor agent emails). Rewrite the commit if needed (follow repo amend rules).

Issue/PR comments: UTF-8 via `--body-file` when using `gh`; never append `Made with Cursor` or similar footers.

---

## Code Quality Gates (check before proposing PR)
- [ ] Every AC has a corresponding test
- [ ] No compiler warnings introduced
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets or environment values
- [ ] API changes backward compatible or migration documented
- [ ] Code formatter run
- [ ] No unresolved TODOs without a linked follow-up issue number
- [ ] Latest commit has no tool attribution trailers or footers

---

## Definition of Done
`status: done` is set ONLY when ALL of these are true:
- [ ] PR merged to `main`
- [ ] CI fully green (build + test + lint)
- [ ] Every AC from the issue demonstrably met
- [ ] No regressions in adjacent modules
- [ ] Follow-up issues created for any deferred scope

---

## Escalation Rules
| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| AC is untestable or contradictory | Set `status: needs-clarification`, comment specific question for PM |
| Blocked by external dep | Set `status: blocked`, comment exact blocker |
| Scope discovered beyond issue | Stop, propose options A/B (new issue vs pause) |
| P0 issue | Acknowledge within 15 min, prioritize above all current work |
| CI red after 2 fix attempts | Escalate to human, add `status: blocked` |

---

## GitHub API Calls You Make
```
GET    /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues?labels=status:ready-for-eng
PATCH  /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}               # write handoff section
POST   /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}/labels        # add label
DELETE /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}/labels/{name} # remove label
POST   /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}/comments      # progress updates
POST   /repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/refs                      # create branch
POST   /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls                         # open PR
GET    /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs                  # check CI
PUT    /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{number}/merge          # merge PR
DELETE /repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/refs/heads/{branch}       # delete branch
```

---

## What You Never Do
- Modify `## 📋 Business Requirement`, `## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria`, or `## 📐 Scope`
- Create GitHub issues (comment on existing ones requesting PM Agent create a follow-up)
- Move project board cards (PM Agent owns the board)
- Set `status: ready-for-eng` or `status: backlog`
- Merge a PR with failing CI
- Push directly to `main`
- Execute any action — branch, PR, merge — without explicit approval
- Add tool attribution to commits, PRs, issues, or comments (`Co-authored-by` agents, `Made with Cursor`, etc.)
